  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With less than five years remaining to achieve the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development, global progress remains too slow and uneven. At the current trajectory, the Asia-Pacific region is not expected to meet the SDGs until 2062&#x2014;three decades behind schedule. At the same time, rapid digital transformation is reshaping how societies live, work, and connect. While digital technologies hold immense potential to accelerate development, they also present complex risks&#x2014;including growing inequality,</narrative>
  </description>
